  "body": "## What changed\n\n2D Chamfer has a `Tip offset` setting. A positive offset moves the cone axis toward physical air and lowers its virtual tip by `(tip offset + chamfer width) * tan(angle)`. The selected cone band runs from the tip offset to the tip offset plus chamfer width. The declared `EdgeBreak` stays on the original selected edge with the authored width and depth.\n\nClosed loops and selected open chains support the setting. Generation refuses a wrong Side, material crossing, excessive tool radius or flute reach, and an offset that folds or loses any selected boundary span. The partial-collapse refusal covers a narrow branch disappearing while its parent loop survives. Zero offset preserves the complete legacy closed and open `Toolpath`, including floating-point depth bytes.\n\nThe parameter reaches the UI, commands, stamps, project files, and MCP create/edit/read/save/reset. The UI shows the control and derived virtual-tip height. The persisted field remains `minimum_cone_radius`.\n\n## Breaking project-format change\n\nProject format **v79** cannot be opened by v78 readers. The fix commit records the existing format break with a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer. Migration preserves the legacy zero offset; project round trips preserve positive values.\n\n## Review fixes\n\n1. Check every original boundary span after a positive offset; loop count alone is insufficient.\n2. Restore the exact legacy depth calculation on both zero-offset routes. Compare complete results with captured pre-feature paths.\n3. Add before/after control and height-note screenshots below.\n4. Record the reason for each retained test binary below.\n5. Record the format break and correct the body to v79.\n\n## Test binary placement\n\nThese PR binaries remain separate for this fix round. They are not isolated-suite exemptions.\n\n- `crates/motion/tests/chamfer_minimum_radius.rs`: keep the complete closed/open cone-band geometry and refusal fixture in the lowest owning crate, independently runnable from application tests.\n- `crates/app/tests/chamfer_minimum_radius.rs`: keep operation command, tool reach, posting, and project-migration checks together without the MCP server fixture.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_chamfer_minimum_radius.rs`: keep the JSON-RPC create/patch/read/save/reset round trip together with its single isolated server fixture.\n\n## UI evidence\n\nThese are actual production egui parameter forms rendered with the same tilted fixture (A = -90°, width 1 mm, angle 45°, local top 11 mm). The before capture restores only the affected pre-feature UI source from `2fbe6f2fbb33d3be8181ae6097766f2b1415c94e`; the after capture uses the reviewed UI source. The before form has no Tip offset and shows the corner at 10 mm. The after form sets Tip offset to 2 mm and shows the virtual cone tip at 8 mm. Only transparent margins were cropped. Temporary capture code and source restoration were removed; no product or golden PNG changed.\n\n| Form | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Geometry control | ![Geometry control before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/a5449789070b9a0fdab5bee7aa993364729c5a86/3251/geometry-before.png) | ![Geometry control after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/a5449789070b9a0fdab5bee7aa993364729c5a86/3251/geometry-after.png) |\n| Derived height note | ![Derived height note before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/a5449789070b9a0fdab5bee7aa993364729c5a86/3251/heights-before.png) | ![Derived height note after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/a5449789070b9a0fdab5bee7aa993364729c5a86/3251/heights-after.png) |\n\n\n## Validation on final head\n\nHead: `613588b2339ae68e3708c33163823f032b37479d`\nQuick planning base (`upstream/main`): `29488d99c9cdbe32b689f7c0d6d70d8361ef85d7`.\nHeavy planning base and current `upstream/main`: `16115cd06a3694dfadaa57876c050e6d83c8faab`.\n\nAnother session advanced the shared upstream ref during the quick run. Both bases produce the same merge base, `80f1dc364c7ec2ec26860d7e9f76613342997bfd`, and the identical 37-file PR diff, so the selected quick and heavy coverage did not change. The PR head and working tree stayed fixed throughout the gates.\n\n- Focused motion pins: 9 passed in `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test chamfer_minimum_radius`.\n- Mutation proof: `a_partial_branch_collapse_is_refused_even_with_one_surviving_loop` and `a_partial_inlet_collapse_is_refused_even_with_one_surviving_loop` both failed with the boundary-survival block removed (exit 101). `zero_radius_matches_captured_legacy_closed_toolpath` and `zero_radius_matches_captured_legacy_open_toolpath` both failed when depth reverted to `width * tan(angle)` (exit 101). Restoring the fixes returned all 9 tests to green. Complete legacy expectations were captured from `2fbe6f2fbb33d3be8181ae6097766f2b1415c94e`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: **808/808 steps passed**, 0 failed, 0 stalled (72.1 minutes). UI library: 1,543 passed, 8 ignored; the adapter-dependent cases also passed on this host.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: **99 passed, 2 failed, 0 stalled across 101 steps** (51.1 minutes, exit 1). The two failures are listed below. All four repository-pinned expected-failure checks matched their required failures (three for #1950 and one for #2849).\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6/6 steps passed, 11 tests passed, 0 failed or stalled (0.9 minutes).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed (1 minute 43 seconds).\n- Catalog: `example_catalog`: 39 passed, 4 ignored; `example_catalog_adaptive`: 1 passed; `example_catalog_edge_work`: 1 passed. All ran within the final-head quick gate; the 4 ignored `example_catalog` cases also passed in the heavy gate.\n- Goldens: `golden_cl`: 34 passed; `recorded_post_streams`: 5 passed; `solid_law_goldens`: 7 passed. All ran within the final-head quick gate.\n\n## Heavy failures and reviewed-implementation baseline\n\n- `flute_reach::a_ten_mm_flute_names_its_cause_before_the_rapid_findings`: expected 3 rapid findings, observed 9. The fixture uses Offset2D, not Chamfer.\n- `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`: expected 6,228 mesh triangles, observed 5,232. This assertion runs before path generation.\n\nBoth failures reproduced unchanged (exit 101 each) with the reviewed-head production implementation at `91a6a2bd5c15582f59fec538ad990f62be348496`. The comparison temporarily restored only `crates/motion/src/machining2d/chamfer.rs`, the only production file changed in this fix round; other production files already matched the reviewed head. The final file was then restored byte for byte and `git diff` was clean.\n\nExact baseline commands:\n\n```text\ncargo test --release -p camcraft-app --test flute_reach a_ten_mm_flute_names_its_cause_before_the_rapid_findings -- --ignored --exact\ncargo test --release -p camcraft-app --test pocket3d_hsm the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean -- --ignored --exact\n```\n\nThese two existing failures are left unchanged because this round fixes only the five review findings.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The catalog and reachable CL, post-stream, and solid-law golden suites ran successfully. No recorded NC/CL program or `examples/catalog/**` file changed; the existing example-project edit changes only the format version.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo manual full-application click-through was performed. The production Geometry and Heights forms were rendered for the before/after evidence. `graphify update` could not run because `graphify` is not on `PATH`.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Chamfer can select a tip offset and cut through that cone band while preserving the authored chamfer width.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3153\n",
